What:		/sys/class/leds/<led>/aura_mode
Date:		September 2026
Contact:	Marco Scardovi <scardracs@disroot.org>
Description:	read/write
		ASUS Aura topology mode on hid-asus Dynamic Lighting nodes.
		One of "auto", "unified", or "split". Writing selects the
		stored mode; reading shows the stored value with the active
		choice in brackets (e.g. "[auto] unified split").

		auto resolves to split: keyboard and lightbar nodes (when
		present) accept effect/direct writes independently, and the
		global node returns -EBUSY. unified inverts that: only the
		global node is writable. Direct RGB may be backed by HID
		LampArray (Usage Page 0x59) when Aura 0xBC cannot address the
		lightbar independently; firmware animations stay on Aura 0xb3.
